---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro'
import ActionBox from '../../components/ActionBox.astro'
import StatusRow from '../../components/StatusRow.astro'
import ServiceEntitlement from '../../components/ServiceEntitlement.astro'
---

<Base
  title="The Studio viewer"
  description="The SMART Studio viewer: read a SMART Recommendation as a model, with tree, code, inspect, and compliance views, the mapping and diff lenses, and validation. Public, no account; the editor is the roadmap program."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Services"
    title="The Studio viewer"
    lede="A SMART Recommendation is a model, and the Studio is where you read it as one: the requirement tree, the code, the mappings, the diff between editions, all validated, all in the browser. It is read-only and public; authoring is the editor program on the roadmap."
  />

  <section class="px-8 pb-20 max-w-5xl">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] mb-4">What it is</h2>
      <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft mb-4">
        The read-only viewer over the published SMART models. Open a Recommendation and move between its lenses: the model tree and its code view, the registry of its artifacts, the mapping lens that aligns editions and related documents, the diff that shows exactly what changed, and a certificate preview. The viewer validates what it shows and says so (the <em>valid</em> marker is computed, not asserted), and it is honest about its posture: <em>read only</em>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Authoring is a separate program, the SMART Studio editor (TODO.editor in the platform program): the package as the unit of work, provenance-carrying saves, the authoring surfaces. When it ships, the Studio stops being read-only; until then, this page says viewer and means it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] mb-4">Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Recommendation authors checking their model as a reader will meet it; reviewers and committee members who want the requirement structure rather than the PDF; toolmakers confirming what the published model actually contains before they build on it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] mb-4">Where it lives</h2>
      <ActionBox
        href="https://www.oimlsmart.org/studio/view/"
        label="www.oimlsmart.org/studio/view/"
        description="The viewer. Public, no account; pick a model and switch lenses."
      />
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] mb-4">How to get access</h2>
      <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        There is nothing to request: open the link and browse. The authoring surface's repository is public (<a href="https://github.com/primmel/editor" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">primmel/editor</a>, source available, license pending) for toolmakers who want to follow the editor program.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] mb-4">Status</h2>
      <StatusRow rows={['studio-viewer']} />
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem)] font-medium tracking-[-0.01em] mb-4">Who can use it, who can run it</h2>
      <ServiceEntitlement service="studio-viewer" />
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-rule pt-8 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Verified 2026-08-29: the viewer answered live and rendered a published model with its read-only and valid markers, the lens bar (model, registry, mapping, diff, certificate preview), and the tree/code/inspect/compliance views.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
